      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2240,
        1936
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 528,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## 09-07-01 food safety temperature log with ai alerts\n\n### How it works\n\nRestaurant health inspections require a written temperature log for every fridge, freezer and hot hold unit, and kitchen staff skip it because filling paper sheets by hand is tedious. This workflow makes the log write itself.\n\n- A temperature reading posts to the webhook from any source: a Google Form, a phone, or a wireless sensor.\n- The workflow validates the reading, an AI assistant checks it against safe temperature ranges, and every reading is logged to Google Sheets.\n- When a temperature is out of range the manager is alerted on Telegram and Discord with the corrective action.\n- Every day at noon it checks whether any reading was logged today and nudges the kitchen if the log is empty.\n- Every Monday it emails the owner a plain-language weekly summary of totals and out of range events.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Create a Google Sheets spreadsheet with a Temperature Log sheet and an Errors sheet, then set the document id in the four Sheets nodes.\n- Point the webhook at any form, app or sensor that can POST JSON.\n- Set the Telegram chat id and Discord channel to your team, and the Gmail recipient to the owner.\n- Add an OpenAI (or compatible) credential and select the model in the two AI nodes.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Change the safe ranges in the AI system prompt to match your local health code.\n- Adjust the noon check and weekly report schedules.\n- Add a cleaning log sheet and reuse the same intake pattern."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
